From 198a34f3b845b3444e21e9a505af6dc35e3f027e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:01:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/66] x86 IPA-RA: never summarize a body another TU can
 replace at link time

'.weak' reach the object through module.symbol_attrs / toplevel_asm, not
IrFunction::is_weak, so the weak body was summarized and callers kept live
values in registers the strong replacement clobbers (red: use() printed 55
instead of 79 at -O1/-O2, no-pic/PIE/PIC). module_opaque_symbols collects
weak or default-visibility symbol_attrs and every identifier named by
top-level asm (C name and asm label); IpaRaState refuses to summarize them.

Tests: 2 unit tests (every route; local visibilities stay summarizable;
an opaque symbol is never summarized) and the multi-TU fast gate
check_ipa_ra_interposition.sh (strong overrides clobbering r8-r11, plus a
static positive control that must keep its IPA keep mask).

(cherry picked from commit 4d845f254546d2e67218e254c48cd7f3a137a47b)
