Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:41:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/66] x86 peephole: make FPO dead callee-save elimination
 fire, with exact CFI

The pass never fired on real code: every emitted push/pop carries CFI
and the call gate refused all non-leaf functions. Rewritten per
.cfi_startproc: a frame-preserving form (prologue subq grows by 8k, the
post-prologue %rsp and every slot are unchanged; frame < 4096 so no
stack-clash probe is needed) and a shrinking form for call-free bodies
without %rsp data. CFA lines are rewritten by formula, surviving
.cfi_offset slots recomputed, superseded same-address CFA rows
collapsed. Refuses foreign CFI, realignment and non-mirror epilogues.
Census: 11 dead saves in 7 functions -> 0; gdb unwound registers equal
actual ones across the rewritten zstd_count main.

(cherry picked from commit 8c47aaadb0043e442b7eeaa50b16151a25eb3bfd)
