From e0087e9b3d719d1851594f66637b12d155cfbcbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:54:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/66] vectorize: psadbw byte-sum reductions at SSE2 and AVX2

The byte-count reduction counted only 0/1 predicates, and only with AVX2.
It now sums any lane-exact byte value with psadbw(lane, 0), at the widest
legal width (ymm/32 with AVX2, xmm/16 on baseline x86-64; i686 excluded):

  * Predicate: 0/1 trees, `& 1` on the packed side (unchanged semantics);
  * Unsigned:  lane-exact trees with range within [0, 255] -- the tree in
               both worlds;
  * Signed:    range within [-128, 127] -- the packed lane is biased by
               `^ 0x80` (exact: v + 128 in [0, 255]) and the exit subtracts
               128 per consumed byte.

Lane exactness is structural (byte_value_tree_is_lane_exact), not
range-based: the range system models a PACKED compare as the mask
(-1, 0) while the scalar value is 0/1, so `0 - (p[i] == 7)` would pass a
range-only check; compares and mask conjunctions in value position are
refused, as is MinMax (the scalar mirror cannot express it).  A constant
trip count below two packed iterations stays scalar.

The vector loop has ONE induction variable: the exit test becomes
`byte_iv OP ext64(limit / W) * W` (W > 0 makes the scaling monotone and
injective in i64, so the predicate is kept with its signedness), and the
resume index is the byte IV.  The old counter feeds only itself and is
removed by DCE: 6 instructions per 16 bytes (movdqu, psadbw, paddq, add,
cmp, jl) instead of 7, and no shl/cltq/movslq resume conversion.

Backend: VecSadbwU8x16 (psadbw, commutative), register-class and
copy-coalescing entries, and VecSadbwU8x16/VecAddI64x2 as vector-register
candidates.

Measured (Callgrind, -O2, baseline x86-64, together with the next commit):
affine_countdown 95.76M -> 20.32M Ir (GCC 16.2 47.76M, Clang 23.1.3
47.95M, ICX 2026.2 43.18M); sieve 142.13M -> 100.88M (GCC 142.10M).
70-program geomean 0.974; no codegen regression (the only positive
deltas are on byte-identical assembly).

Tests:
  * vectorize_byte_sum_tests.rs: builds the loop IR for 12 shapes x
    accumulator/IV types x constant/dynamic limits, runs the transform,
    and executes BOTH worlds in an interpreter that models the packed
    intrinsics lane by lane (and faults on any read past n); the result
    must equal the scalar loop at both widths.  Mutation-checked: a wrong
    bias shift and a zero-extending signed remainder each fail it.  Plus
    refusals, the trip-count floor, width selection and classification.
  * vec_byte_sum_reduction{,_avx2}.c: every shape and five must-refuse
    shapes through the real backend, lengths 0..299 at all 16
    misalignments, extreme bytes, wrapping seeds, the affine global form.
  * check_byte_count_normalize.py: the baseline-ISA and no-AVX arms must
    now EXERCISE the SSE2 psadbw form (they only forbade vpsadbw), and a
    kill-switch arm covers the SSE2 path.
