Subject: [PATCH 13/66] ci: require an SSE2 -m32 GCC oracle for the i386
 default-mode vector ABI gate

The i386 default-mode contracts compare lccc's default i686 vector ABI
(SSE2: 16-byte GNU vectors in %xmm, matching Clang 23.1.3's pentium4
default and the pinned tag-cache GCC 16.2 build) against the oracle's
default.  A distribution GCC configured --with-arch-32=i686 (Debian sid's
gcc-16) passes those vectors on the stack, so both gates failed locally
while hosted CI (tag-cache GCC 16.2, verified identical to the local
gcc-16-ce prefix) was green: the verdict measured the packaging.

gcc_oracle_require_m32_sse2 makes that precondition explicit and fails
with a configuration diagnostic naming the fix (the pinned prefix from
scripts/ci_install_gcc_oracle.sh) instead of reporting an ABI mismatch.
The local i686 gate also ran ahead of `asm-diff-oracle-gas-2.47` and so
took whatever `as` was on PATH (Debian's 2.44; the script refuses it).  It
now runs right after that provisioning gate and puts the pinned prefix on
PATH, exactly as the hosted ipa-lrs.yml step does.  No second invocation of
ensure_gas_247.sh: the parity checker and the corpus-contract tokenizer
police the single registered one.

Since main's i686-gnu-vector-abi rewrite (PR #946 port) passes explicit
ISA flags (-msse2 / -march=i686 / -mno-sse) to every compiler on every
leg, that gate no longer depends on the oracle's -m32 default and does not
take the precondition; check_gnu_vector_align_abi.sh Part 3 still builds
with bare -m32 and does.
