Subject: [PATCH 16/66] vectorize: exact byte-sum predicate masks and
 constant-trip loops

Follow-ups to the psadbw byte-sum reduction (bc09c910d), measured on the
sieve counting loop and the f_const kernels:

* Predicate counts sum the raw lane mask: psadbw adds 255 per set lane,
  so the exit divides once by 255 (exact) instead of masking every vector
  with `& 1`.  A `!=` count packs one `==` compare and the exit takes
  `consumed - count(==)` (no pcmpeqd/pxor NOT per vector); `m != 0` over
  a lane mask folds to `m`.
* The count normaliser rematerialises an in-body `GlobalAddr` stream base
  in the preheader (`if (g[i]) c++` over a global array stayed scalar:
  LICM runs after the normaliser).  push_preheader_inst keeps the span
  table in step for an empty preheader (it tested emptiness, not length).
* Constant trip count (constant limit >= one vector): the packed loop is a
  guard-free do-while exiting from the latch, the remainder starts at the
  constant packed byte count (no trunc/sext of the byte IV), and it is
  bottom-tested, or elided when limit % W == 0.  Before, backend layout
  rotation emitted `xor %r8d,%r8d; cmp $E,%r8; jge` plus a remainder entry
  test and a movslq.
* Every insertion in the transform keeps the positional span table in
  step (spanned_insert/spanned_push): codegen reads line info by index.
* Census-neutral splits: byte_map_cmp out of parse_byte_map_expr,
  byte_sum_trees and byte_sum_exit_insts out of the transform,
  widening_index_casts/body_symbol_name out of normalize.

Tests: interpreted constant-trip matrix (every remainder 0..=W, 4 IV
types, 6 kinds, both widths, structure asserted) plus a span-step check
over the whole interpreted matrix; vec_byte_sum_const_trip{,_avx2}.c
(225/137 loops transformed, GCC 16.2 output oracle).
