From 006ec3c1281e6a2e61a2f24f0b76a8cc3d2da174 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:49:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/66] peephole: cross-block upper32-zero proof via CFG
 must-dataflow

`upper32_zero_at` stopped at the first label, so a 32-bit writer in a
dominating block could never license dropping a zero-extending copy
(`movl %esi,%r8d; movb %dl,(%rdi,%r8)`) after a loop header or join.

At a label the query now consults a per-function forward must-analysis
over the existing liveness CFG (`classify` + `resolve_jump_tables`; an
unresolvable indirect jump makes the function unknown): a 16-bit GP mask,
entry = 0, unreached = 0, `out` initialised to ALL, Gauss-Seidel in
program order (Jacobi hit the round cap: quadratic cost and lost
precision).  The transfer kills every written family and re-proves only
through `s_write_proves_upper_zero`; calls, inline asm, pinned lines and
non-inert directives kill all.  Results are memoised by function content
hash (two generations).

Cost control, each measured with Callgrind on the 10-program compile set:
- narrow_copy_fold asks the proof lazily, only for the first use that
  needs W64 (was: eagerly before the cheap rejects);
- exact fallthrough fast reject (one killing predecessor path refutes a
  must-fact) before locating/hashing the function;
- `may_write_families`: `writes_family`'s definition as one mask per line
  instead of 16 re-parses (unit-tested equal per family);
- an exact prefilter for `s_write_proves_upper_zero` (tested implication);
- an exact cross-solve transfer cache keyed on text, verified on the full
  `(LineInfo, text)` key (LineInfo now derives PartialEq/Eq outside tests).
Compile Ir vs the series without this commit: +1.385% total (Jacobi
+5.06%), worst gzip_longest_match +5.04% (one 600-line function, 116
queries across rewrites); output asm unchanged by the cost work.

Runtime Ir vs the same series (outputs identical): histogram -9.46%,
zstd_double_fast -6.06%, gzip_longest_match -5.88%, zstd_count -3.24%,
ascii_case_fold -3.08%, lz4_compress -2.16%, ra01_global_match -1.97%,
linux_list_sort -0.43%; no program worse.
