split_label_offset split at the first separator whose tail parsed as ONE
integer, so `movl ca+16+4, %edx` recorded R_386_32 against a symbol named
`ca+16` (addend 4), `4+ca` against `4+ca` and `ca+8-4` against `ca+8`:
undefined at link time, or silently wrong bytes in hand-written asm. The
x86-64 encoder already uses the shared relocation grammar and matched
GAS 2.47 on all seven probed forms; i686 now consults it first and keeps
the old scan only for what that grammar declines (`x@indntpoff+4`).

Pre-existing on main: tests/regression/global_init_pointer_scalar_base_m32.c
failed at `-m32 -O2 -fno-pie` with "undefined symbols: ca+16, ca+24"
(i686 codegen emits `movl ca+16+4, %edx` for a 64-bit global's high half).
The corpus under -fno-pie goes 1156/1 -> 1157/0. Unit tests cover the
splitter and assemble the three spellings end to end, checking both the
relocation symbol and the folded REL displacement bytes against GAS.
