From a8d18c6e962b2870ed340c10a2c67be78b012c4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:57:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/66] x86 SSE2: shuffle-free zero-extension split for
 constant-guarded widening sums

VecWidenMaskedAddValueI32x4ToI64x2 (e6bab609e) re-splatted a constant guard
through %eax every iteration (`movl $K,%eax; movd; pshufd`) and always took
the dual sign-unpack (psrad + 2 punpck). Two exact improvements:

* A constant K compares against a 16-byte-aligned .rodata splat
  (lane_const_rip_operand pools are .p2align 4, as legacy-SSE pcmpgtd m128
  requires): no in-loop materialisation.
* For K >= -1 every surviving lane is >= 0, so sign- and zero-extension
  agree. The I64x2 accumulator is only ever horizontally summed
  (VecHorizontalAddI64x2; NEON's VecSadalpI32x4 already accumulates
  pairwise), so split each qword instead of unpacking: lo = q & 0xffffffff
  ({a0,a2}), hi = q >> 32 ({a1,a3}). pand + psrlq replace a zero register
  and two shuffle-port punpcks. K < -1 and run-time guards keep the
  sign-unpack (negative lanes survive).

Loop body per 4 elements, `if (a[i] > 0) s += a[i]`: 14 -> 12 instructions
and 3 -> 0 shuffle uops. Callgrind Ir (4096 x 20000, outputs identical):
>0 308.1M -> 246.7M, >1000 349.1M -> 246.7M, >-5 349.1M -> 287.6M; GCC
16.2 -O3 410.0M, Clang 23.1.3 -O3 307.9M/389.8M, ICX 2026.2 246.3M/328.2M
(ICX uses the punpck form with a hoisted zero, unrolled x2).
loop_patterns benchmark -2.50% Ir; the other 73 programs are byte-identical.

check_sse2_widening_4lane_sum.sh: the `sum_positive` psrad assertion pinned
a provably redundant instruction; it now requires the pand/psrlq split, and
adds K = 1000 (.rodata compare, no in-loop splat) and the K = -5 control
(sign-unpack REQUIRED, no psrlq split). Fails on the parent.
