From 86e04cd4e35ca43d795185440e08b2f50d15ee05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:54:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/66] i686: scalar FP honours the resolved SSE/SSE2/SSE3
 floor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pre-existing defects, all reproduced: i686 F32 arithmetic, compares and
casts used SSE2 without SSE2 (-march=i686, -mno-sse2); `fisttp` (SSE3) was
emitted on the default -m32 baseline (x86-64-v1 = SSE2, no SSE3; GCC 16.2
and Clang 23.1.4 both default to pentium4); `movups` leaked under
-march=i686; and nothing stopped such leaks reaching the object.

Codegen: `sse2_scalar_enabled` / `fisttp_enabled` follow the resolved ISA
(new CodegenOptions i686_no_sse2 / i686_no_sse3). Without SSE2, F32 binops
and compares use x87 (fcomip+seta, GCC's shape); without SSE3 truncating
stores switch only the RC field around fistp (fnstcw / orw $0x0c00 / fldcw
/ fistp / fldcw — GCC's sequence). F64 -> <=i32 uses `cvttsd2sil` straight
from memory under SSE2 (GCC's form; was ~20 instructions).
`emit_f32_load_to_x87` treats a register home as authoritative and pushes
F32 constants as immediates; `emit_f64_load_to_x87` no longer clobbers
%eax for constants (pushl $imm halves, fldz/fld1 for exact +0.0/1.0 bit
patterns only) and fails closed instead of silently leaving the x87 stack
one short when a value has no slot (floats are never GPR-allocated).

Driver: `resolved_i686_sse{,2,3}()` are the single source of truth; the
final-text fences are keyed on them (not on codegen policy), skip user
inline asm, and name the offending function and instruction.

Evidence (objdump census of the fixture objects):
  -march=i686 / -mno-sse2: 0 xmm, 0 fisttp, 18 fistp
  default -m32:            56 xmm, 0 fisttp, 5 cvttsd2si
  -msse3:                  56 xmm, 8 fisttp, 0 fistp
qemu-i386 -cpu pentium2 runs the no-SSE builds and SIGILLs the SSE ones
(TCG traps only the no-SSE level; SSE2/SSE3 are covered by the fences).

Tests: four `i686_scalar_fp_isa_*` corpus fixtures (one shared .inc; GCC
16.2 output-equality per mode), emitter tests for the permissions, the RC
switch and the constant loads, the SSE3 fence vocabulary test.
