MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`int s; for (...) if (a[i] > k) s += a[i];` never vectorized: before
if_convert the guard is a body branch (the early run rejects the internal
CondBranch), and the late rerun admitted only min/max plus the guarded
I32->I64 widening sum. The equal-width shape is the same structural case
— upstream's own rationale ("the ONLY reduction shape the early run can
structurally never see in transformable form") applies verbatim — and its
AVX2 lowering, VecMaskedAddI32x8, already existed but was unreachable.
The adler32 concern behind the gate is about UNGUARDED sums the early run
declined on judgment; those stay out. Without AVX2 the SSE2 reduction path
still refuses guarded equal-width sums (no masked composite), so they stay
scalar there. The recogniser's obligations are unchanged and were probed:
the guard must compare the summed loaded element (swapped arms refused);
a loop-variant rhs (`a[i] > b[i]`, `a[i] > i`) is refused downstream.

