  int, `> t`      86.05M -> 13.96M     (GCC -O2 10.85M,        Clang 7.40M)
  program        292.30M -> 71.40M     (GCC -O2 128.03M, -O3 52.78M)

Test: vector_guard_sum_equal_width.c — every vector-width boundary trip
count, misaligned bases, >=/mirrored spellings, INT_MIN/INT_MAX guard and
element edges, run-time guards, the widening sibling. UBSan-clean (GCC;
Clang with -fsanitize=integer); GCC/Clang/lccc agree at -O0..-O3, -m32.
