Subject: [PATCH 30/66] vectorize/x86: I64x4 AVX2 widening accumulator;
 interleave late masked loops

AVX2 I32->I64 widening sums accumulated into a half-width I64x2 home, so
every step paid a 128-bit fold and the loop ran at half the vector width.
The widening steps (VecWidenAddI32x4ToI64x4 / VecWidenMaskedAddI32x4ToI64x4)
now fold `vpmovsxdq` straight into a YMM I64x4 accumulator (regalloc class
8). Unmasked: `vpmovsxdq MEM,%ymm0; vpaddq`. Masked: the I32 guard runs on
the 128-bit load before the sign extension (exact because the compare mask
is all-ones/all-zeros per lane). `fold_ymm0_into_i64x4_acc` handles every
accumulator/destination home combination (the old fold dropped `dest` for
mixed homes). The SSE2 value-shaped I64x2 ops are unchanged.

VecMaskedAddI32x8 writes a YMM register but never re-armed
`dirty_upper_ymm`, so the function epilogue could omit `vzeroupper`; it
now sets it, and it accepts the interleaver's displacement argument.

Pipeline-order defect: the guarded sums are only vectorized by the late
vectorizer entries (they need if_convert's Select form), but
`vec_interleave` runs once, right after the EARLY vectorizer, so every
late loop stayed single-accumulator (one loop-carried vpaddd/vpaddq
chain). `vec_interleave::run_late` runs after both late entries and their
DCE, admitting only loops whose accumulator steps are late-only ops; the
early run structurally never produces them, so early loops and the
verbatim epilogues their interleave left behind are never re-sliced (the
pass has no idempotence marker). Same `vec_interleave` kill switch, and
verify_after_pass("vec_interleave_late").

