From ef97fc3803809ddb007f791488e38d893680f494 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:39:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/66] x86/vectorize: guarded i32 sums - SSE2 masked step,
 hoisted guards, home-complete folds

Conditional sums `if (x[i] > k) s += x[i]` now vectorize on every x86-64
level with Clang-23-quality inner loops.

* SSE2 equal-width guarded sum: new `VecMaskedAddValueI32x4` (acc, lanes,
  guard) lowered to `pcmpgtd`/`pand`/`paddd` (legacy SSE, scratch
  xmm0-2; `pmaxsd` only with SSE4.1 for a zero guard). Interleavable in the
  late rerun next to its widening sibling.
* Loop-invariant guard splats are hoisted into the loop's unique preheader
  (never block 0): the broadcast is pure, the rhs is re-checked loop
  invariant, and an out-of-loop definition dominates the preheader. The
  masked steps compare against the homed splat directly - no per-step
  `movd` + `pshufd`/`vpbroadcastd`.
* Zero guard (`x > 0`) on AVX memory-shaped steps folds the lane load into
  `vpmaxsd mem, %zero, %ymm0` + `vpaddd` (2 uops/8 lanes, Clang 23's loop);
  a slot-homed zero falls back to the constant-0 form.
* Home-complete accumulator folds. The old folds keyed on the accumulator's
  slot: a homed accumulator feeding a slot destination fell into
  `vpaddd %ymm0,%ymm0,%ymm0` (doubled lanes), a slot accumulator never
  wrote a homed destination, a constant accumulator emitted nothing.
  `fold_xmm_parts_into_acc` (128-bit) and `fold_ymm0_into_acc_256` (one
  3-operand add straight into the destination home, Const = zero identity)
  now serve every masked/widening step.
* SSE2 `VecBroadcastI32x4` writes its home directly; `VecBroadcastI32x8`
  no longer stages through `vmovd` twice.
* NEON: the shared SSE2/NEON transform's Sum arms are guard-blind, so a
  guarded reduction now fails closed before reaching it (verified: never
  reached by any guard fixture or the benchmark kernels at -O2/-O3, so no
  AArch64 output changes on those inputs).
* A dangling guard `Select` is no longer left behind in the vector body.

