From c7eff6a100d07696d16a274d39e1887643d25a71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:09:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/66] regalloc: integer horizontal sums are scalars with GPR
 homes

`produces_vector_value()` listed `VecHorizontalAddI64x4`, which returns a
scalar i64 (`movq %xmm0, %rax`) exactly like its I32x8/I32x4/I64x2
siblings. `collect_non_gpr_values` therefore poisoned the whole copy web of
the result: after an AVX2 widening reduction (`long s += int[i]`) the
scalar remainder kept its accumulator in a stack slot (`vmovq %xmm0,
8(%rsp)`, then `addq %r10, 8(%rsp)` per element: a load-add-store chain).
No `class_of` producer row or consumer list depended on the dest being a
vector; only the result-side classifications change.

On x86-64 the four integer horizontal-sum results also become GPR-eligible:
each emitter lands its result with the register-aware `store_rax_to` and
uses only %rax/%xmm0/%xmm1 as scratch, none of them allocatable, so the
result coalesces with the tail web instead of bouncing through a slot.
Other backends' lowerings are not audited for this contract and keep the
old behaviour.

