From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:54:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/66] x86 peephole: dead frames under callee-saved pushes;
 exact CFI on every row

`remove_dead_leaf_frame` only matched a prologue that was exactly
`subq $N, %rsp`. Once integer horizontal sums got GPR homes, `wsum`
(artifacts bench) kept `pushq %rbx; subq $16, %rsp` with no line
referencing the frame, and a census of the 21 tests/bench kernels at -O2
found 4 of 83 functions in that shape (bench_run x2, put_varint,
utf8_scan): two dead instructions per call.

Generalise the pass to frame-pointer-omitted prologues with k >= 0
callee-saved pushes before the `subq`. An epilogue is an
`addq $N, %rsp` followed by exactly k pops and `ret`; every `ret` must
reach one backwards through those pops; any other push/pop, inline asm
or `%rsp` mention declines. The WO-1 ret-pairing argument carries over:
each path crosses the prologue `subq` and exactly one collected `addq`,
the pushes and pops are untouched. With calls, the frame shrinks to the
smallest N' with 8 + 8k + N' = 0 (mod 16) (8 for even k, 0 for odd k);
a misaligned original declines.

Pre-existing CFI defect fixed on the way: only the first
`.cfi_def_cfa_offset` after the `subq` was rewritten, but the codegen
restates the full-frame CFA after every mid-body `ret` for the block
that follows. A multi-exit dead-frame leaf therefore kept
`.cfi_def_cfa_offset N+8` there while `%rsp` sat at CFA-8, so gdb, perf
and -fexceptions unwinding read the return address from the wrong slot.
Every row equal to the frame total is now rewritten; rows inside the
push region stay; any other value, `.cfi_def_cfa`, `_register` or
`.cfi_adjust_cfa_offset` declines before anything changes. Rows that
then restate the running CFA are dropped (CFI is linear in address
order; functions with remember/restore_state are left alone).

Tests (whole peephole pipeline, as the file requires): the multi-exit
CFI regression, pushes + two exits with the exact CFA row sequence, the
odd-k delete and even-k shrink call frames, and five refusals
(misaligned call frame, short epilogue, stray body pop, frame-pointer
prologue, foreign CFA value).
