Subject: [PATCH 47/66] target_clones: give resolvers a live next_label

`build_target_clones_resolver` mints its blocks from the lowerer's global
label counter but published `next_label: 0`. The ordinary and nested
function constructors publish `self.next_label`. The invariant on
`IrFunction::next_label` is that every live label is below it, so any later
pass that mints a label in a resolver could reuse a live one. With
CCC_VERIFY_IR=abort, upstream's own fixture failed in every build since
the feature landed:

  [ir-verify] after `lowering(pre-O2)` in `vec_add_reduce.resolver`:
    stale label counter: next_label=0 but live max label is 45

The resolver now publishes `self.next_label`, as its siblings do.

The T6 gate (check_verify_ir_clean.sh) samples every 25th corpus file and
never reached this fixture. The sampled list is regenerated by script and
must not be hand-edited, so the gate now appends a small pinned list of
regression files, checked the same way.
