From ceae2ceb1c60c271bd5342301aa972908fe3b76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:47:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 51/66] regalloc: an FP copy-web leader must be scan-eligible

fp_copy_web_groups unions Copy-connected scalar FP values; the merge
seeds the XMM scan with one interval per web (the envelope of the
members that carried scan intervals) under the union-find root as
leader, and spreads the leader's register over those members. Members
filtered out of the scan (call-spanning, zero-length) correctly keep
their own home -- but the leader was never checked. A call-spanning
root therefore entered the scan with an envelope that does not cover
its own call, was homed in a caller-saved XMM, and the call clobbered
it; the peephole then (correctly) deleted the dead result move.

Reproducer: an F32 call result live across a later call and copied
into a phi web on one arm (tests/regression/fp_copy_web_call_leader.c,
reduced from scripts/fuzz_float_scalar_vs_gcc.py seed 197). Wrong
output at -O1 and above on ms178/lccc main 2031eddd7 (the bug predates
this series); the default-mode fuzz found 5 divergences in 960 runs
there (seeds 197 and 203), 0 after this change.

The leader is now the root when it is eligible -- every web that was
already correct allocates byte-identically -- and otherwise the
smallest eligible member; the root keeps its own home and its copies
stay real moves.
