From 500a60563d7533b157db349f97c62a746c62d801 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:36:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 56/66] div_by_const: divide by the type minimum with a
 compare, not idiv

`x / INT_MIN`, `x % INT_MIN` and the LLONG_MIN forms fell through every
strength-reduction arm (the negation of MIN does not fit) and emitted
`idiv`, which is 10-18 cycles and not pipelined on Golden Cove and Zen 4.
Every dividend except MIN itself has a smaller magnitude than MIN, so:

  x / MIN  ==  (x == MIN)          (I64: the int compare widened)
  x % MIN  ==  (x == MIN) ? 0 : x

Neither can trap: MIN / MIN is 1 and MIN % MIN is 0. The quotient is
GCC 16.2's `cmp`/`sete`; the remainder is `cmp`/`cmov`, where GCC 16.2
emits seven instructions. llvm-mca (block reciprocal throughput, cycles):
remainder 6.0 -> 2.5 (alderlake) and 24.0 -> 1.5 (znver4); quotient
3.0 -> 1.5 and 12.0 -> 1.0.

An I64 division by INT_MIN is an ordinary negative power of two and keeps
the shift path; `is_signed_type_min` is exact per width so it is never
caught here.

Tests: a unit test evaluates both widths at every boundary and pins the
expansion to <= 2 instructions; `sdiv_srem_type_min.c` (and its -m32
sibling, where the I64 forms are register pairs) checks the values
against GCC, including the MIN dividend.
