Subject: [PATCH 57/66] i686: _mm_stream_si64 stores both halves of a constant

The i686 Movnti64 lowering loaded its own operand: from a slot it read
both words, but for a constant it stored the low word and a zero high
word. So `_mm_stream_si64(p, -1)` wrote 0x00000000ffffffff, and every
negative or >= 2^32 constant was truncated. It now uses the shared pair
loader (`emit_load_acc_pair`), which handles every 64-bit operand form
(wide slot, narrow slot, register, both halves of a constant via
`pair_const_bits`), and stores %eax/%edx with two MOVNTIs.

`movnti64_i686.c` checks constants -1, -2, 2^32+1 and INT64_MIN plus two
variables. The s162 binary fails four of them. It is lccc-only
(LCCC_NO_COMPARE): GCC has no 64-bit MOVNTI in 32-bit mode, so the
self-check is the oracle.
