From dae12762e0d3736e69f55b566b1ec2e8bcb5371e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:24:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/66] x86: __m64 is GCC's 8-byte vector type

lccc's `__m64` was `struct { long long __val; }`. On x86-64 the psABI
classes that struct INTEGER, so lccc passed and returned `__m64` in GPRs
(`movq %rsi,%rax` for `__m64 f(__m64 a, __m64 b) { return b; }`) while
GCC and Clang use `%xmm` (SSE class, `movdqa %xmm1,%xmm0`). Every
`__m64` call across a GCC/Clang-built boundary exchanged garbage.

`__m64` is now GCC's definition,
`int __attribute__((__vector_size__(8), __may_alias__))`. The intrinsics
work on its 64-bit image through `(long long)` / `(__m64)(long long)`
bitcasts, which lccc keeps in a register: on x86-64 both directions
compile to a single `movq`, as in GCC. On i686 lccc never enables MMX, so
`__m64` follows GCC's `-mno-mmx` ABI (memory), as the struct already did
there; the gate pins that equivalence.

`_mm_extract_pi16` took `&(A)`, so an rvalue operand
(`_mm_extract_pi16(_mm_add_pi16(a, b), 1)`, which GCC accepts) failed to
compile; it is now a pure shift of the 64-bit image. The MMX differential
generator gained rvalue operands for extract, insert and shuffle. The
direct-call lowering of `_mm_stream_pi` reads the vector's storage
instead of the struct's.

`check_public_simd_abi.py` / `boundary.c` gain a BITS=64 leg: nine
`__m64` arguments around an `__m128` (overflowing the eight XMM argument
registers), a 64-bit scalar, direct, indirect and variadic calls, in all
four caller/provider pairings at -O0 and -O2, on x86-64 and on i686 with
`-mno-mmx` for both compilers: 160 legs (was 144). The previous compiler
fails every x86-64 leg in which lccc is caller or provider.

`vec8_abi_sse1_only{,_o0}.c` gain the `__m64` shapes under
`-mno-sse2 -msse`: `_mm_stream_pi` of a parameter, `__m64` arguments and
results, `{__m64}`, an indirect call and a ninth `__m64` on the stack
(GCC `6265d4f34ddddfda`).
