From cd8988fb839c48c8c7aae3fa29d6177c42eea883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:24:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 64/66] vector builtins: __builtin_shufflevector of any width;
 typeof of shuffles

lccc accepted `__builtin_shufflevector` only for two 4 x 32-bit operands
and four indices, and rejected the rest of GCC 12+/Clang's contract. It
now follows GCC 16.2 (probed): two vectors with the same element type
(lane counts may differ), one integer constant index per result lane into
their concatenation, -1 for "any lane", and a power-of-two index count.
The result has the operands' element type and one lane per index
(`CType::with_lane_count`). Rejections use GCC's wording. Clang ext
vectors (no GCC equivalent) follow Clang and take any index count: three
indices on a `float4` give a `float3` (`CType::shufflevector_result`).

The 4 x 32-bit to 4-lane shape keeps its PSHUFD / typed-home path
unchanged. Every other shape is a lane gather through the lane helpers,
which know padded ext-vector strides, x87 lanes and bit-packed bool
lanes. A result of at most 8 bytes follows `__builtin_shuffle`'s
convention: the packed register value on x86-64, the object's address
everywhere else.

`typeof` of either shuffle builtin fell back to `int` with only a warning
(sema's cache does not cover `typeof` operands, and the lowerer's
fallback did not know the builtins), so
`__typeof__(__builtin_shuffle(a, m)) x = ...` silently truncated. Both
sema and the lowerer now type the call through one shared function,
`CType::shuffle_builtin_result`.

`shufflevector_any_width{,_m32}.c` cover narrowing, widening,
mixed-width operands, 1- to 32-lane results, 1/2/4/8-byte integer and
float/double lanes, packed results in conditionals, arguments, returns,
casts and compound assignment, the retained 4 x 32-bit path, and
compile-time `typeof` sizes. The i686 leg uses `-mno-mmx`: with MMX
enabled, i386 GCC returns 8-byte vectors in `%mm` registers without
EMMS, and its next x87 operation yields the default NaN.
`shufflevector_ext_vector{,_m32}.c` (lccc-only, values from Clang
23.1.4) cover 3-lane results and padded 3-lane operands.
`check_shuffle_diagnostics.sh` pins the new rejection classes (signedness
mismatch, non-power-of-two count, index -2) against GCC.
