From faadbbe83784a0a5c5d90072084b5d41fbb2bb40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:27:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 65/66] x86 headers: set intrinsics without signed-shift UB

The C bodies of the MMX/SSE2/AVX2 set intrinsics built 64-bit lane
words as `(long long)(unsigned T)x << 32` (also << 48 and << 56). That
signed shift overflows whenever the top lane has its sign bit set, which
is undefined behaviour (C11 6.5.7p4): under `-fsanitize=undefined
-fsanitize-trap=undefined`, `_mm_set1_pi8(-1)`, `_mm_set_pi32(-1, 0)`
or `_mm_setr_epi16` with a negative fourth lane trapped, where GCC's
builtin-based headers run clean. It was found by running the regression
fixtures that include these headers in UBSan trap mode.

The lane words are now built from unsigned 32-bit halves, joined once.
That also keeps i686 out of 64-bit shift chains on register pairs, and
the byte/word broadcasts become one multiply by 0x01010101/0x00010001.
llvm-mca, 100 iterations, alderlake/znver4 cycles, old -> new:

  x86-64 _mm_set_pi32    306/204 ->  109/105
  x86-64 _mm_set_pi8    1507/904 ->  810/605
  x86-64 _mm_set1_pi8    369/394 ->  112/109
  x86-64 _mm_setr_epi16  721/558 ->  524/561
  i686   _mm_set_pi8   3917/10262 -> 2119/6141
  i686   _mm_set1_pi8  2718/7048  ->  926/5161
  i686   _mm_setr_epi16 3469/5507 -> 1785/2273
  i686   _mm_set_epi8  6918/11007 -> 3521/4706

Costs: x86-64 `_mm_set_epi8` with 16 variable bytes goes 1563/1613 ->
1624/1715 (the constant form is unchanged), and i686 `_mm_set_pi32`
goes 1118 -> 1218 on alderlake (znver4 unchanged). Rejected, with
data: a vector literal stores bytes and reloads a qword (a
store-forwarding failure on both cores), and an unsigned 64-bit chain,
while UB-free, is slower than the halves on every target.

`simd_set_lanes_ubsan{,_m32}.c` call every set form with negative,
positive and minimum top lanes under UBSan trap mode and compare with
GCC; the old headers trap at -O0, -O2 and -m32.
